+/**
+ * @fileoverview amxts: objects made in the frame of the function that makes them.
+ *
+ * An object that never leaves the function that makes it - its fields read
+ * and written there, its address given only to an import that keeps none -
+ * is made in that function's own part of the shadow stack instead of the
+ * heap: nothing is allocated, and nothing is left for the collector. Run on
+ * the optimized module, where the code that makes an object (a constructor,
+ * a getter that returns a new one) is inlined into the code that uses it.
+ *
+ * Such an object has the header of a static one: transparent, so the
+ * collector neither frees it nor looks inside. The collector reads every
+ * word of the shadow stack as a reference, so the frame's objects start with
+ * a mark and the bytes the function took, which it steps over (itcms.ts,
+ * visitStack). That is safe because nothing
+ * inside it can be a reference to another object: a 32-bit word stored into
+ * it is a constant or an address of the object itself, and any other store
+ * of a reference would come with the collector's barrier, a call that is
+ * given the object - which makes it leave.
+ *
+ * A function that may suspend (an async function's coroutine, parked by an
+ * import) is left as it is: a parked coroutine's frames are copied into an
+ * array the collector reads as references.
+ *
+ * @license Apache-2.0
+ */
+
